// ⚠ `typecheck` uses THIS config, not `tsconfig.json`, and the difference is the
// test file.
//
// `tsconfig.json` excludes `src/**/*.test.ts` because a test must not land in
// `dist`. But `pnpm typecheck` reading the same config would then check every
// line of this package EXCEPT its 380-line suite — and `vitest` runs through
// esbuild, which strips types without checking them. So a type error in the
// suite would be invisible to every gate.
//
// That is not hypothetical drift: this module was `packages/client/src/lib/
// flow-authoring.ts` until foundations Phase 2.1, where the client's own
// `tsconfig.json` (`include: ["**/*.ts"]`) did typecheck the suite. Mirroring
// `@foundry/redact`'s two-line config exactly would have quietly dropped that on
// the way across.
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": { "noEmit": true },
  "include": ["src/**/*.ts"],
  "exclude": ["node_modules", "dist"]
}
